# Likeness Looter: "{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card" and "{X}: This creature becomes a copy of target creature card
# in your graveyard with mana value X, except it has flying and this ability. Activate only as a sorcery." Bot1 loots
# away Argothian Elder on turn 3 and Embereth Shieldbreaker on turn 5, then pays X=2: with X announced first (CR
# 601.2b-c) the Elder, of mana value 4, is no legal target, and the Shieldbreaker is. The Looter becomes an Embereth
# Shieldbreaker with flying - a 2/1 red Human Knight - and stays one past the end of the turn: the effect states no
# duration (CR 611.2b). On turn 7 it has no loot ability (the Shieldbreaker's text has none) but has "this ability":
# X=4 makes it an Argothian Elder - a 2/2 green Elf Druid with "{T}: Untap two target lands" - with flying.

